      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## QuantFunc LTX-2.5\n\n- **QuantFunc LTX-2 Loader** replaces the official `Load Diffusion Model` (UNETLoader): the QuantFunc engine runs the LTX-2.5 22B distilled transformer, video and audio; the Gemma text encoder (`CLIPLoader`, type `ltxv`), the video and audio VAEs and the sampler stay stock ComfyUI.\n- `transformer`: `ltx-2.5-22b-distilled-quantfunc-int4-r128.safetensors` from ModelScope [QuantFunc/LTX-2.5-QuantFunc-4bit](https://modelscope.cn/models/QuantFunc/LTX-2.5-QuantFunc-4bit), in `models/diffusion_models`.\n- From Hugging Face [Lightricks/LTX-2.5](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.5) (accept its license first): text encoder `gemma4-12b-with-proj-ltx-2.5-comfy-int8-convrot.safetensors`, VAEs `ltx-2.5-video-vae-bf16.safetensors` and `ltx-2.5-audio-vae-bf16.safetensors`.\n- The distilled model runs with CFG 1 and the fixed sigma list in `ManualSigmas`. Any sampler works; the loader keeps the audio clean. `pinned_memory` is ON by default on this loader.\n- Frame count: 8k+1 (97 = 4 s, 121 = 5 s at 24 fps); width and height: multiples of 32.\n\n**Text to video with audio**, one pass at 768x512, 97 frames (4 s at 24 fps).\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## QuantFunc LTX-2.5\n\n- **QuantFunc LTX-2 Loader** replaces the official `Load Diffusion Model` (UNETLoader): the QuantFunc engine runs the LTX-2.5 22B distilled transformer, video and audio; the Gemma text encoder (`CLIPLoader`, type `ltxv`), the video and audio VAEs and the sampler stay stock ComfyUI.\n- `transformer`: `ltx-2.5-22b-distilled-quantfunc-int4-r128.safetensors` from ModelScope [QuantFunc/LTX-2.5-QuantFunc-4bit](https://modelscope.cn/models/QuantFunc/LTX-2.5-QuantFunc-4bit), in `models/diffusion_models`.\n- From Hugging Face [Lightricks/LTX-2.5](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.5) (accept its license first): text encoder `gemma4-12b-with-proj-ltx-2.5-comfy-int8-convrot.safetensors`, VAEs `ltx-2.5-video-vae-bf16.safetensors` and `ltx-2.5-audio-vae-bf16.safetensors`.\n- The distilled model runs with CFG 1 and the fixed sigma list in `ManualSigmas`. Any sampler works; the loader keeps the audio clean. `pinned_memory` is ON by default on this loader.\n- Frame count: 8k+1 (97 = 4 s, 121 = 5 s at 24 fps); width and height: multiples of 32.\n\n**Text to video with audio**, one pass at 768x512, 97 frames (4 s at 24 fps).\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
